  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The TOP BYPASS VALVE was designed to extend pump runtimes by ensuring flow to the pump if the intakes plug off from sand, scale, or paraffin deposits.",
   "box": {
    "x": 600,
    "y": 264,
    "w": 598,
    "h": 48
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The Top Bypass Valve is installed at the top of the bottom hole assembly. If a pressure differential greater than 33 psi is reached, the valve opens, bypassing the plugged intakes, allowing continued production.",
   "box": {
    "x": 600,
    "y": 336,
    "w": 598,
    "h": 72
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The Top Bypass Valve can be used in combination with any OSI system.",
